 4. 🕔 After hours: GTA flu outbreak 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Grand Theft Auto VI is advertised for sale at a game store in Hong Kong today. Photo: Vernon Yuen/Nexpher Images via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The initial reviews for Grand Theft Auto VI — released early this morning and expected to be the biggest entertainment hit of the year — are rolling in ... and they're breathless. 

 🗣️ A sampling :

 NYT : It "largely lives up to its sky-high expectations by inverting the series's reputation for destruction." WaPo : "It is a great gathering of art forms and talent, an unruly, comprehensive cultural atlas of American life and manners." IGN : "I see no real limit to the amount of time I could spend here, endlessly exploring and interacting with Vice City and the massive area surrounding it." The Verge : "The buildup to Grand Theft Auto VI's launch is unlike anything the game industry has ever seen. Even more remarkable? The game was actually worth the wait." 💰 By the numbers: The publicly traded Take-Two Interactive — which makes GTA through its Rockstar Games unit — got about 20 million pre-orders for the game, according to HSBC Global Investment Research analyst Mohammed Khallouf.

 Khallouf today raised his 2027 GTA sales forecast from 40 million units to 52 million. 🤒 The bottom line: If you called in sick with the "GTA flu" to play the game today, you have company.

 Silicon Valley company Logitech provided a new floating holiday for workers to play video games — and about 70% of one manager's entire team took it today, per NYT . 
 
